// 2788
[struct_2788]
param=param_2095,Agrith Naar
param=param_2096,33
param=param_2153,npc_14502
param=param_2168,npc_14503
param=param_2123,37
param=param_2124,31
param=param_2097,3
param=param_2184,This big demon came to Gielinor in one of the early ages and is an ancient being with a great wealth of experience in battle.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Shadow of the Storm<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Watch out! Agrith Naar will attack with melee and magic, switching depending upon your use of the protection prayers. Agrith Naar will also occasionally teleport you towards him, so attacking from a distance isn't always so easy. You must deal the finishing blow with Silverlight (provided in the arena).
param=param_2102,Grrrrr
param=param_2118,sound_4427
param=param_2119,sound_4427
param=param_2120,sound_4427
param=param_2121,sound_4427
param=param_2122,6000
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,domtower_icon_agrith_naar

// 2789
[struct_2789]
param=param_2095,Dagannoth Mother (version 1)
param=param_2096,34
param=param_2153,npc_14613
param=param_2168,npc_14619
param=param_2123,37
param=param_2124,31
param=param_2097,1
param=param_2184,This is the first dagannoth mother to scare those living in Rellekka; a creature that features predominantly in children's stories among the Fremennik. This nightmare of a sea creature is, unfortunately, very real.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Horror from the Deep<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Is anything ever better than the original? Well, this version of the mother changes from one protective type to another in a set order. Remember, to deal damage, consider its colours: blue (water magic); orange (melee attacks); green (ranged attacks); brown (earth magic); red (fire magic); white (air magic). She attacks with melee and ranged, depending on how close and personal you wish to get.<br><br>If you don't have the normal spellbook active, it will become active when you start this battle, and will revert afterwards.
param=param_2102,Nrraaa
param=param_2118,sound_8362
param=param_2119,sound_8362
param=param_2120,sound_8362
param=param_2121,sound_8362
param=param_2122,9000
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_dagannoth_mother

// 2790
[struct_2790]
param=param_2095,TokTz-Ket-Dill
param=param_2096,35
param=param_2153,npc_14568
param=param_2168,npc_14570
param=param_2123,37
param=param_2124,31
param=param_2097,1
param=param_2183,npc_14569
param=param_2184,This creature has a carapace of obsidian as its initial defence mechanism. In the TzHaar language its name relates to it being an armadillo guarded by obsidian armour and they know just how deadly it can be. Any combatant needs to break through its armour while avoiding its mace-like tail before standing a chance of damaging it.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: TokTz-Ket-Dill<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: TokTz-Ket-Dill is immune to ranged and magic and, before you start dealing any damage, you'll want to mine through its thick armour (pickaxe provided in arena). Once broken, the TokTz-Ket-Dill is weak to crushing weapons. The beast will attack with melee and occasionally stomp the ground to rain rocks on your head.
param=param_2102,Grrrr
param=param_2118,sound_7973
param=param_2119,sound_7973
param=param_2120,sound_7973
param=param_2121,sound_7973
param=param_2122,15000
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_toktz

// 2791
[struct_2791]
param=param_2095,Black, Grey and White Golems
param=param_2096,36
param=param_2153,npc_14594
param=param_2154,npc_14595
param=param_2155,npc_14596
param=param_2168,npc_14597
param=param_2169,npc_14598
param=param_2170,npc_14599
param=param_2123,39
param=param_2124,33
param=param_2125,38
param=param_2126,32
param=param_2127,39
param=param_2128,31
param=param_2097,2
param=param_2184,These creations are next to mindless. Following the instructions of their creators they will attack anything that comes near them unquestioningly. Their distinct colours are the only clues to their inner workings.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Spirits of the Elid<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: For all three golems, magic and ranged attacks are dramatically reduced. For the black golem you're best using crushing attacks; for the white golem you're best using stabbing attacks and for the grey golem you should use slashing attacks.
param=param_2102,Destroy human
param=param_2103,As my master wills it
param=param_2104,Death to you
param=param_2118,sound_8635
param=param_2119,sound_8635
param=param_2120,sound_8635
param=param_2121,sound_8635
param=param_2122,16500
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_bwg_golems

// 2792
[struct_2792]
param=param_2095,Treus Dayth
param=param_2096,37
param=param_2153,npc_14488
param=param_2154,npc_14491
param=param_2155,npc_14491
param=param_2156,npc_14491
param=param_2168,npc_14489
param=param_2169,npc_14492
param=param_2170,npc_14492
param=param_2171,npc_14492
param=param_2123,38
param=param_2124,31
param=param_2125,39
param=param_2126,33
param=param_2127,40
param=param_2128,31
param=param_2129,39
param=param_2130,29
param=param_2097,2
param=param_2184,Treus is the guardian of the dangerous crystals in the haunted mine below the river Salve, or at least he was until he died - and now it's his spirit that lingers on. This supernatural being has the ability to possess and control objects around him. Luckily in this tower it's 'only' pickaxes any combatant has to worry about.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Haunted Mine<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: The more damaged Treus is the more likely he is to show his cowardly nature and run from you, fading and teleporting away. Hit him to turn him back into his true form. He attacks (when he's not running away) with melee. He is also accompanied by three possessed pickaxes.
param=param_2102,Your death is imminent
param=param_2103,
param=param_2104,
param=param_2105,
param=param_2118,sound_2901
param=param_2119,sound_2901
param=param_2120,sound_2901
param=param_2121,sound_2901
param=param_2122,4500
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_treus_dayth

// 2793
[struct_2793]
param=param_2095,Elvarg
param=param_2096,38
param=param_2153,npc_14547
param=param_2168,npc_14548
param=param_2123,36
param=param_2124,30
param=param_2097,1
param=param_2184,The giant green dragon of Crandor, Elvarg was awoken on the island by an adventurer and anyone nearby soon suffered her wrath. One person she didn't kill was Melzar. A pretty unforgettable chap.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Dragon Slayer<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Possibly one of the most famous dragons to ever live, Elvarg attacks with a mixture of melee and dragon fire breath. You better have a anti-dragonbreath shield with you if you want to limit the damage you receive.
param=param_2102,Roaar
param=param_2118,sound_4656
param=param_2119,sound_4656
param=param_2120,sound_4656
param=param_2121,sound_4656
param=param_2122,9000
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_elvarg

// 2794
[struct_2794]
param=param_2095,Culinaromancer
param=param_2096,39
param=param_2153,npc_14515
param=param_2168,npc_14516
param=param_2123,38
param=param_2124,32
param=param_2097,3
param=param_2184,A lunatic chef that was once renowned for his culinary creations in Lumbridge Castle. His insane drive for domination soon came to light and he was imprisoned. Having broken free, he needs to be stopped before he carves someone up with that vicious looking meat cleaver he carries.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Recipe for Disaster<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: This twisted chef will attack with magic. Not so strong without his minions to protect him now!
param=param_2102,No more meals for you, fool
