param=param_463,mutated jadinkos
param=param_460,109
param=param_462,These warped jade vine creatures will not hesitate to use their environment to help them in combat if they cannot retaliate otherwise. The baby jadinkos are easiest to kill, but the males offer the greatest rewards. Ranged weapons made from vines are best against them.
param=param_465,90
param=param_466,80
param=param_659,npc_13821

// 28870
[struct_28870]
param=param_463,Vyrewatch
param=param_460,110
param=param_462,These foul creatures can be found throughout Meiyerditch and Darkmeyer in Morytania. They have a telepathic ability which enables them to dodge incoming attacks, so you'll need a weapon specially created to harm them.
param=param_466,0
param=param_659,npc_4837

// 28871
[struct_28871]
param=param_4832,Seiryu's Intervention
param=param_4833,As the Ambassador continues to summon in floods of invulnerable Crassian Ritual Keepers, with seemingly no way to defeat them, Seiryu intervenes. After appearing at the side of the arena, Seiryu will <col=FFFFFF>fully heal</col> all players and use a <col=FFFFFF>Deep Breath</col> attack to destroy the Crassians.
param=param_4834,npc_26067

// 28872
[struct_28872]
param=param_4832,Circle of Black Hands
param=param_4833,In his fury, Kranon decides to call upon Xau-Tak for the final phase of the fight. This causes 12 Black Hands to appear and they immediate begin projecting dark magic towards Kranon in order to heal him and empower him.<br><br>It is possible to intercept the projectiles, causing minor <col=FFFFFF>typeless</col> damage to yourself instead of allowing them to heal the Ambassador.
param=param_4834,npc_26069

