// 30560
[struct_30560]
param=param_4832,Stage One
param=param_4833,When the Araxxi encounter begins, you'll be contained within a starting area.<br>To progress you must pick one of the two burnable webs to set fire to. After a minute the web will burn away and you can progress to stage two. The webs you can burn change every four days.<br><br>In this stage Araxxor can <col=FFFFFF>Cocoon, Cleave</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Web Shield.</col><br><br>There are three types of styles that Araxxor can spawn in, <col=FFFFFF>Ranged</col> represented by <col=FFFFFF>green legs</col>, and will apply a poison dot throughout the fight, <col=FFFFFF>Magic</col> represented by <col=FFFFFF>blue legs</col>, and damage throughout the fight will slowly drain stats and lower overload timers and <col=FFFFFF>Melee</col> represented by <col=FFFFFF>red legs</col>, and will apply a damage over time effect that increases randomly throughout the effect's lifetime.

// 30561
[struct_30561]
param=param_4832,Cocoon
param=param_4833,When fired, you will become encased in webbing. The more you click the more you will break free. Using the ability <col=E6DCB4>Freedom</col> or <col=E6DCB4>Anticipation</col> before this attack will help lower the amount you are cocooned for.
param=param_4835,seq_24083
param=param_4836,seq_24084
param=param_4837,model_96806

// 30562
[struct_30562]
param=param_4832,Web Shield
param=param_4833,A web shielding will cover the boss for 10 seconds. While this is present, the boss will take half damage and reflect half damage to you. If you don't attack, the boss will heal while the shield is present.
param=param_4835,seq_24075
param=param_4836,seq_24061
param=param_4837,model_96809

// 30563
[struct_30563]
param=param_4832,Cleave
param=param_4833,The boss will pull you towards them if you haven't used the <col=E6DCB4>Freedom</col> or <col=E6DCB4>Anticipation</col> ability. Cleave will hit massive damage to anyone caught in front of the boss.
param=param_4835,seq_24050
param=param_4836,seq_24053
param=param_4837,model_96805

// 30564
[struct_30564]
param=param_4832,Stage Two
param=param_4833,After the web has burned away, you can venture down your chosen path. Depending on what path you choose, Araxxor will gain new attacks. You'll have to deal with these before progressing to Stage Three.

// 30565
[struct_30565]
param=param_4832,Burn spawn
param=param_4833,In all paths, Araxxor will spawn a few eggs which will hatch into aggressive spiders if not dealt with. Luckily he'll also launch a fiery projectile towards you. If this explodes on the eggs it will destroy them - enraging the boss!
param=param_4835,seq_24085
param=param_4836,seq_24086
param=param_4837,model_96803

// 30566
[struct_30566]
param=param_4832,Path One: More Spiders!
param=param_4833,If you take the top path, Araxxor will try and spawn spiders to help kill you. Other than standard spiders, he can spawn a <col=FFFFFF>pulsing spider</col> that will heal him while it lives, and a <col=FFFFFF>mirrorback spider</col> that will make the boss reflect all damage while the mirrorback is alive.

// 30567
[struct_30567]
param=param_4832,Path Two: Acid Spiders
param=param_4833,If you take the middle path, Araxxor can fire a projectile at the floor leaving an acidic puddle on the floor for ten seconds. <br><br>After this time the puddle will form into an acidic spider that will rush towards you, exploding for massive damage after a short amount of time or if it touches you.
param=param_4835,seq_24046

// 30568
[struct_30568]
param=param_4832,Acidic Ramp
param=param_4833,On path two you must degrade the ramp to progress to Stage Three. To do this you must have Araxxor stay in the acid pool to absorb the acid.<br><br>You need him to have at least half the acid to degrade the ramp - note that it will drip off him if he isn't in the pool.

// 30569
[struct_30569]
param=param_4832,Darkness
param=param_4833,If you take path three, Araxxor will plunge the entire area into darkness which will inflict increasing damage over time if you do not stand in the light beams.

// 30570
[struct_30570]
param=param_4832,Charge
param=param_4833,Roughly every minute in path three, Araxxor will drop down from the ceiling and charge you. If you make an attempt to dodge he'll smash into the wall behind.<br><br>Dodging in the correct direction prevents you from taking damage and causes the most damage to the wall, with only two being required for the wall to cave in.
param=param_4835,seq_24113

// 30571
[struct_30571]
param=param_4832,Stage three: Finish him!
param=param_4833,On entry to stage three, Araxxor will prioritise finishing off any path mechanics you didn't finish. He may spawn acid spiders if you chose path two and spiders if you chose path one.<br><br>On top of this, the path you didn't pick will become active, so those attacks will occur in stage 3 until Araxxor dies.

// 30572
[struct_30572]
param=param_4832,Stage four: Araxxi
param=param_4833,After you have defeated Araxxor, Araxxi will consume him. Araxxi will use any left over attacks (such as acid or spider minions) as well as performing <col=FFFFFF>Cleave, Web Shield</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Cocoon</col>.<br><br>As Araxxi drops below 50% health she will stop doing special attacks and instead grow increasingly damaging.<br><br>As Araxxi goes below 25% health (or 35% in duo), she will enrage faster and spawn an acid wave that tracks the target down until they are hit. When the acid wave hits, it will remain on the target until they move away, at which point it will bounce away and start again.
param=param_4835,seq_24047
param=param_4836,seq_24048
param=param_4837,model_96826

// 30573
[struct_30573]
param=param_4832,The Crypts
param=param_4833,In the Barrows, there are six barrow mounds. Each leads to a crypt which contains one of the infamous Barrows Brothers. One of the brothers won't be present and instead his grave will give access to the area beneath the crypts.<br><br>In the area beneath the crypts you'll have a chance to encounter any brothers you've not killed. Navigating to the centre will grant access to the reward chest.<br>The more Barrows Brothers you kill, the better chance you'll have to receive loot!

// 30574
[struct_30574]
param=param_4832,Ahrim the Blighted
param=param_4833,Ahrim is a mage of great strength and will attack with powerful fire spells.<br>There is a 1/4 chance with every attack that Ahrim will drain your Strength level.
param=param_4835,seq_1165
param=param_4836,seq_674
param=param_4837,model_3098
param=param_4834,npc_2025

// 30575
[struct_30575]
param=param_4832,Dharok the Wretched
param=param_4833,Dharok wields a massive greataxe. As he attacks you, he'll hit harder the lower his life points are. Protecting for melee or staying at a distance is recommended.
param=param_4835,seq_2067
param=param_4834,npc_2026

// 30576
[struct_30576]
param=param_4832,Guthan the Infested
param=param_4833,Guthan uses his warspear to sap health from his victims. With every attack there is a 1/4 chance he'll heal what he hits!
param=param_4835,seq_2080
param=param_4834,npc_2027

// 30577
[struct_30577]
param=param_4832,Karil the Tainted
param=param_4833,Karil is a strong ranger and uses his repeating crossbow to deal damage. There is a 1/4 chance he'll drain your Magic level if he hits you.
param=param_4835,seq_2075
param=param_4834,npc_2028

// 30578
[struct_30578]
param=param_4832,Torag the Corrupted
param=param_4833,Torag uses his massive hammer to smash his foes. There is a 1/4 chance his melee attacks will drain 5% of your Adrenaline.
param=param_4835,seq_2068
param=param_4834,npc_2029

// 30579
[struct_30579]
param=param_4832,Verac the Defiled
param=param_4833,Verac wears unholy armour that grants his warmace a 1/4 chance to ignore his opponent's armour!
param=param_4835,seq_2062
param=param_4834,npc_2030

// 30580
[struct_30580]
param=param_4832,Akrisae the Doomed
param=param_4833,Akrisae the Doomed is located north in Verac's tomb. Those who fight him should be prepared - he can pray against your attacks and switch styles in reaction to your attacks.
param=param_4835,seq_2068
param=param_4834,npc_14297

// 30581
[struct_30581]
param=param_4832,The Shadow Realm
param=param_4833,At the start of the encounter, the shadow binds the brothers together. If a brother is defeated, you must defeat another within 30 seconds or the shadow will revive all brothers to fight once more. Defeating a brother will also reset the revive timers of other brothers, and it will heal any brother still standing.<br><br>At the start of the fight one brother will be more in contact with the Shadow Realm and there is a chance he will send all players to the Shadow Realm at a point in the fight.<br><br>Inside the Shadow Realm, all special attacks the brothers perform will have increased accuracy and damage.<br>Be warned! If no-one is present on one side of the encounter, the shadow will send all brothers to the other side, when they are all back up.

// 30582
[struct_30582]
param=param_4832,Ahrim
param=param_4833,Ahrim will use standard fire attacks against his opponent that have a 1/8 chance to drain Strength levels. He also uses the <col=FFFFFF>Flight, Telejump, Shadow Pits</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Turret of Fire</col> special attacks.

// 30583
[struct_30583]
param=param_4832,Ahrim: Flight
param=param_4833,When Ahrim drops below 90% life points, he'll take the air. When flying, Ahrim will only use standard attacks against you. While flying Ahrim is immune to melee damage and takes 50% magic damage.

// 30584
[struct_30584]
param=param_4832,Ahrim: Telejump
param=param_4833,Ahrim will Telejump to a pillar in the centre of the arena and begin attacking the other side of the encounter - as well as lighting all the shadow pits on the other side.
param=param_4834,npc_18538
param=param_4835,seq_21917
param=param_4836,seq_14402
param=param_4837,model_59585

// 30585
[struct_30585]
param=param_4832,Ahrim: Shadow Pits
param=param_4833,When Ahrim sets a pit to shadow, it'll glow brightly and hurt anyone caught in it. There is a 1/8 chance Ahrim's pit will be red. Any brother that walks in a red shadow pit will heal.

// 30586
[struct_30586]
param=param_4832,Ahrim: Turret of Fire
param=param_4833,Ahrim will teleport to a spot in the room and ignite his hands. As he rotates on the spot, anyone caught in the flames will take heavy fire damage.<br>
param=param_4834,npc_18538
param=param_4835,seq_21911
param=param_4836,seq_21912
param=param_4837,model_91464

// 30587
[struct_30587]
param=param_4832,Dharok
param=param_4833,Dharok uses damaging melee attacks that get far stronger the fewer life points he has.<br><br>Dharok can use the <col=FFFFFF>Greatest Axe, Wall Slam,</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Hurricane</col> special attacks.

// 30588
[struct_30588]
param=param_4832,Dharok: Greatest Axe
param=param_4833,Dharok raises his greataxe for <col=FFFFFF>10</col> seconds, storing any damage in it that is done against him. After the 10 seconds, he'll unleash it on his next attack!
param=param_4834,npc_18540
param=param_4835,seq_21940
param=param_4836,seq_21952
param=param_4837,model_91541

// 30589
[struct_30589]
param=param_4832,Dharok: Wall Slam
param=param_4833,Dharok runs to a nearby wall, runs up it and then flings himself towards his original target, slamming down for massive damage.
param=param_4834,npc_18540
param=param_4835,seq_21948

// 30590
[struct_30590]
param=param_4832,Dharok: Hurricane
param=param_4833,Dharok starts spinning wildly towards his opponent, hitting all nearby with his greataxe for heavy damage.<br>
param=param_4834,npc_18540
param=param_4835,seq_21941
param=param_4836,seq_21953
param=param_4837,model_79068

// 30591
[struct_30591]
param=param_4832,Guthan
param=param_4833,Guthan uses his warspear, which has a 1/8 chance to heal an amount equal to his hit.<br><br>Guthan can use the <col=FFFFFF>Impale, Hurricane,</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Throw</col> special attacks.

// 30592
[struct_30592]
param=param_4832,Guthan: Impale
param=param_4833,Guthan will try to throw his spear at a player he isn't targetting. If the spear impales the target they will bleed for heavy damage, until they run to Guthan and he pulls it back out of them.
param=param_4834,npc_18541
param=param_4835,seq_21944

// 30593
[struct_30593]
param=param_4832,Guthan: Hurricane
param=param_4833,Guthan starts spinning wildly towards his opponent, hitting all nearby with his warspear for heavy damage.
param=param_4834,npc_18541
param=param_4835,seq_21941
param=param_4836,seq_21953
param=param_4837,model_79068

// 30594
[struct_30594]
param=param_4832,Guthan: Throw
param=param_4833,Guthan will try to locate Ahrim, Karil, or Verac to throw them. If successful, he'll <col=E6DCB4>Surge</col> over to them and throw them to a random nearby location, inflicting damage to anyone near where they land.<br>
param=param_4834,npc_18541
param=param_4835,seq_21929

// 30595
[struct_30595]
param=param_4832,Karil
param=param_4833,Karil uses his twin pistol crossbows to inflict ranged damage. There is a 1/8 chance his attacks will drain Attack and Magic levels.<br><br>Karil can also use the <col=FFFFFF>Portal Dash, Lightning Conductor</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Bombard</col> special attacks.

// 30596
[struct_30596]
param=param_4832,Karil: Portal Dash
param=param_4833,Karil will summon a shadow portal at his location that he uses to dash to the other side of the encounter.<br><br>He will continue jumping side-to-side until he runs out of portals. After <col=FFFFFF>4 seconds</col> the shadow portal will explode, dealing massive damage to those nearby, less if they are further away.<br><br>If you enter a shadow portal you will close it, preventing it from exploding but taking more damage if you have been through portals before.
param=param_4834,npc_18543
param=param_4835,seq_21917
param=param_4836,seq_21918
param=param_4837,model_91461

// 30597
[struct_30597]
param=param_4832,Karil: Lightning Conductor
param=param_4833,Karil will teleport to a spot in the room and unleash shadow-lightning from his hands. As he rotates on the spot, anyone caught in the lightning will take heavy damage.
param=param_4834,npc_18543
param=param_4835,seq_21911
param=param_4836,seq_21912
param=param_4837,model_91463

// 30598
[struct_30598]
param=param_4832,Karil: Bombard
param=param_4833,Karil will teleport to a pillar in the centre of the arena and begin attacking the other side of the encounter - as well as unleashing a massive lightning barrage down a strip of the room on the other side.<br>
param=param_4834,npc_18543
param=param_4835,seq_18224
param=param_4836,seq_21908
param=param_4837,model_91465

// 30599
[struct_30599]
param=param_4832,Torag
param=param_4833,Torag uses his massive hammer to deal melee damage. He has a 1/8 chance to reduce his opponents' adrenaline by 5%, and can use the <col=FFFFFF>Hurricane, Throw, Wall Slam</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Whack</col> special attacks.

// 30600
[struct_30600]
param=param_4832,Torag: Hurricane
param=param_4833,Torag starts spinning wildly towards his opponent, hitting all adjacent with his hammer for heavy damage.
param=param_4834,npc_18544
param=param_4835,seq_21941
param=param_4836,seq_21953
param=param_4837,model_79068

// 30601
[struct_30601]
param=param_4832,Torag: Throw
param=param_4833,Torag will try to locate Ahrim, Karil, or Verac to throw them. If successful, he'll <col=E6DCB4>Surge</col> over to them and throw them to a random nearby location, inflicting damage to anyone near where they land.<br>
param=param_4834,npc_18544
param=param_4835,seq_21929

// 30602
[struct_30602]
param=param_4832,Torag: Wall Slam
param=param_4833,Torag runs to a nearby wall, runs up it and then flings himself towards his original target, slamming down for massive damage.
param=param_4834,npc_18544
param=param_4835,seq_21948

// 30603
[struct_30603]
param=param_4832,Torag: Whack
param=param_4833,Torag will jump into air and smash his opponent from above, pushing them right through the ground! While stuck in the ground, Torag will constantly hit them - until someone else has hurt Torag enough that he stops!<br>
param=param_4834,npc_18544
param=param_4835,seq_21935

// 30604
[struct_30604]
param=param_4832,Verac
param=param_4833,Verac is back with his warmace. He will use standard attacks against you, with a 1/8 chance he'll ignore your armour when hitting.<br><br>Verac can also use the <col=FFFFFF>Wall Slam, Throw, Deathcopter</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Soulspot</col> special attacks.

// 30605
[struct_30605]
param=param_4832,Verac: Wall Slam
param=param_4833,Verac runs to a nearby wall, runs up it and then flings himself towards his original target, slamming down for massive damage.
param=param_4834,npc_18545
param=param_4835,seq_21948

// 30606
[struct_30606]
param=param_4832,Verac: Throw
param=param_4833,Verac will try to locate Ahrim or Karil to throw them. If successful, he'll <col=E6DCB4>Surge</col> over to them and throw them to a random nearby location, inflicting damage to anyone near where they land.<br>
param=param_4834,npc_18545
param=param_4835,seq_21929

// 30607
[struct_30607]
param=param_4832,Verac: Deathcopter
param=param_4833,Verac will signal to any of his brothers than he can launch in the next <col=FFFFFF>20 seconds</col>. If another brother tries to <col=FFFFFF>Throw</col> Verac in this time he will instead take to the air and track his opponent. Should he get to them he'll smash down for incredible damage.
param=param_4834,npc_18545
param=param_4835,seq_21942

// 30608
[struct_30608]
param=param_4832,Verac: Soulspot
param=param_4833,Verac will tie his opponent's soul to a random point in the environment, marked by green arrows. Until his opponent stands on this spot, Verac will constantly sap their prayer points.<br><br>

// 30609
[struct_30609]
param=param_4832,The Escape
param=param_4833,After the brothers have been defeated, you have to leave to claim any malevolent energy. As you leave the encounter area, it will begin to collapse, you and your team have <col=FFFFFF>30 seconds</col> to escape before it implodes.

// 30610
[struct_30610]
param=param_4832,Confusion
param=param_4833,The Chaos Elemental confuses his opponents, teleporting them to a random area around him unless they are more than 20m away.
param=param_4835,seq_5443

// 30611
[struct_30611]
param=param_4832,Discord
param=param_4833,The Chaos Elemental lets chaos decide when discord hits. When it meets its target, it will randomly act as a melee, ranged, or magic attack and hit as such.
param=param_4835,seq_5443

// 30612
[struct_30612]
param=param_4832,Madness
param=param_4833,If you have space in your inventory, the Chaos Elemental may use Madness against you. Madness aims to remove your main-hand weapon and up to three items in random slots.
param=param_4835,seq_5443

// 30613
[struct_30613]
param=param_4832,Melee attack
param=param_4833,Commander Zilyana smashes her sword against her target for heavy damage. There is a <col=FFFFFF>50%</col> chance when Zilyana attacks in melee that she instead performs her magical attack.
param=param_4835,seq_6964
param=param_4834,npc_6247

// 30614
[struct_30614]
param=param_4832,Magic attack
param=param_4833,Commander Zilyana finds all nearby targets and calls upon Saradomin's lightning to deal heavy magic damage to all it hits.
param=param_4835,seq_6967
param=param_4834,npc_6247

// 30615
[struct_30615]
param=param_4832,Saradomin bodyguards
param=param_4833,Commander Zilyana has backup with her in the form of <col=FFFFFF>Bree, Starlight</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Growler</col>. Each uses a different point of the combat triangle and Commander Zilyana will respawn any dead bodyguards every <col=FFFFFF>30 seconds.
param=param_4835,seq_17497
param=param_4834,npc_6248

// 30616
[struct_30616]
param=param_4832,Lightning: <col=DC7800>Hard mode only
param=param_4833,Commander Zilyana summons a lightning storm on up to five opponents at a time. A lightning storm will move a small amount at random, hitting heavy magical damage to anyone caught in it.
param=param_4835,seq_19949
param=param_4834,npc_17092

// 30617
[struct_30617]
param=param_4832,Ultimate death: <col=DC7800>Hard mode only
param=param_4833,When Commander Zilyana has been defeated for the second time, she can only be killed via use of an <col=FFFFFF>Ultimate ability.</col>. If this does not happen after <col=FFFFFF>6 seconds</col>, she will heal up and continue fighting.
param=param_4835,seq_10419
param=param_4834,npc_17085

// 30618
[struct_30618]
param=param_4832,Melee attack
param=param_4833,The Corporeal Beast will violently swing his feet or stamp them at his target, hitting them for heavy damage with a chance to drain prayer points.
param=param_4835,seq_10058
param=param_4834,npc_8133

// 30619
[struct_30619]
param=param_4832,Magic (single target)
param=param_4833,The Corporeal Beast hit its main target for heavy magic damage, also draining their prayer points, and degrading their summoning and magic levels. (If the targets summoning points are fully drained it will deal extra damage instead)
param=param_4835,seq_10410
param=param_4834,npc_8133

// 30620
[struct_30620]
param=param_4832,Magic (area target)
param=param_4833,The Corporeal Beast fires a magical attack at his current target's position. On impact, it explodes and splits into multiple smaller projectiles - all hitting heavy magical damage to those get caught in the blast.
param=param_4835,seq_10410
param=param_4834,npc_8133

// 30621
[struct_30621]
param=param_4832,Devour
param=param_4833,If the Corporeal Beast senses the presence of a familiar, he will devour it, destroying it completely.
param=param_4835,seq_10053
param=param_4836,seq_10054
param=param_4837,model_41118
param=param_4834,npc_8133

// 30622
[struct_30622]
param=param_4832,Stomp
param=param_4833,Anyone caught standing up the Corporeal Beast will feel his wrath as he violently stomps on them, hitting heavy damage until they move away.
param=param_4835,seq_10496
param=param_4836,seq_10497
param=param_4837,model_42557
param=param_4834,npc_8133

// 30623
[struct_30623]
param=param_4832,Dark core
param=param_4833,As the Corporeal Beast's life points drop, there is a greater chance he will spawn a dark core if one is not present.<br><br>A dark core will lock on to its target and fling itself towards it. Anyone caught on the dark core will take consistent damage that helps heal the Corporeal Beast.
param=param_4835,seq_10392
param=param_4834,npc_8127

// 30624
[struct_30624]
param=param_4832,Dagannoth Rex
param=param_4833,Dagannoth Rex is the melee-based dagannoth king. He can only be hurt by <col=FFFFFF>magic</col> attacks.
param=param_4835,seq_29367
param=param_4834,npc_2883

// 30625
[struct_30625]
param=param_4832,Dagannoth Prime
param=param_4833,Dagannoth Prime is the magic-based dagannoth king. He can only be hurt by <col=FFFFFF>ranged</col> attacks.
param=param_4835,seq_29379
param=param_4836,seq_29380
param=param_4837,model_114236
param=param_4834,npc_2882

// 30626
[struct_30626]
param=param_4832,Dagannoth Supreme
param=param_4833,Dagannoth Supreme is the ranged-based dagannoth king. He can only be hurt by <col=FFFFFF>Melee</col> attacks.
param=param_4835,seq_29372
param=param_4836,seq_29374
param=param_4837,model_114237
param=param_4834,npc_2881

// 30627
[struct_30627]
param=param_4832,Spinolyp
param=param_4833,Spinolyps can spawn all around the king's chamber in the water. They use a combination of magic and ranged attacks, which also have a chance of poisoning the player. Spinyolps can also dive and disappear into the water for a short time before re-emerging.
param=param_4835,seq_2868
param=param_4834,npc_2892

// 30628
[struct_30628]
param=param_4832,Melee attack
param=param_4833,General Graardor punches his main target for massive melee damage.
param=param_4835,seq_17389
param=param_4834,npc_6260

// 30629
[struct_30629]
param=param_4832,Ranged smash
param=param_4833,General Graardor punches the ground in fury, sending the debris from the punch towards targets nearby for ranged damage.
param=param_4835,seq_17391
param=param_4834,npc_6260

// 30630
[struct_30630]
param=param_4832,Bandosian bodyguards
param=param_4833,General Graardor has backup with him in the form of <col=FFFFFF>Sergeant Strongstack, Steelwill</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Grimspike</col>. Each uses a different combat style, and General Graardor will respawn any dead bodyguards every <col=FFFFFF>30 seconds.
param=param_4835,seq_6181
param=param_4834,npc_6261

// 30631
[struct_30631]
param=param_4832,Protection stance: <col=DC7800>Hard mode only
param=param_4833,The general goes into a defensive stance for <col=FFFFFF>10 seconds</col>. During this stance, the general reflects some of the damage he takes if inflicted from the front.
param=param_4835,seq_19844
param=param_4834,npc_6260

// 30632
[struct_30632]
param=param_4832,Graardor smash: <col=DC7800>Hard mode only
param=param_4833,The general smashes his fists into the ground hitting anyone caught for heavy damage. Shortly after the ceiling crumbles down on the targets' locations. Those who can see the collapse risk taking damage from the debris if they are in the vicinity of its fall.
param=param_4835,seq_19843
param=param_4834,npc_6260

// 30633
[struct_30633]
param=param_4832,Phase 1: Melee attack
param=param_4833,The Giant Mole slashes her main target for melee damage.
param=param_4835,seq_22610
param=param_4834,npc_18932

// 30634
[struct_30634]
param=param_4832,Burrow
param=param_4833,The Giant Mole will burrow into the ground and relocate herself to another area in the environment where she'll re-emerge and continue attacking when found.
param=param_4835,seq_22614
param=param_4836,seq_22617
param=param_4837,model_71927
param=param_4834,npc_18932

// 30635
[struct_30635]
param=param_4832,Phase 2B: Rockfall
param=param_4833,The Giant Mole stomps the ground, loosening some of the ceiling. This attack will stun a main target and the mud from above will begin falling on them until they are freed, either by a team-mate or the mole herself.
param=param_4835,seq_22622
param=param_4836,seq_22623
param=param_4837,model_93391
param=param_4834,npc_18932

// 30636
[struct_30636]
param=param_4832,Phase 2C: Berserk
param=param_4833,The Giant Mole goes berserk for <col=FFFFFF>15 seconds</col>. During this time, the mole can be stunned and deals increased damage with increased accuracy.
param=param_4835,seq_22625
param=param_4836,seq_22624
param=param_4837,model_93390
param=param_4834,npc_18933

// 30637
[struct_30637]
param=param_4832,Phase 2D: Mini-moles!
param=param_4833,When the Giant Mole is in the north-western room, she will summon smaller moles to aid her. The Giant Mole gains damage reduction if small moles are alive.
param=param_4835,seq_22607
param=param_4834,npc_18936

// 30638
[struct_30638]
param=param_4832,Har-Aken
param=param_4833,Har-Aken will emerge from the lava every <col=FFFFFF>30 seconds</col>. While it is visible, it can be attacked. After <col=FFFFFF>30 seconds</col> it will submerge once again.
param=param_4835,seq_16233
param=param_4834,npc_15211

// 30639
[struct_30639]
param=param_4832,Tentacles
param=param_4833,While Har-Aken lives, its tentacles will spawn around the platform. These can spawn in <col=FFFFFF>magic</col> or <col=FFFFFF>ranged</col> forms, getting too close will allow them to <col=FFFFFF>melee</col> the target. These should be defeated to keep incoming damage as low as possible.
param=param_4835,seq_16252
param=param_4834,npc_15210

// 30640
[struct_30640]
param=param_4832,Standard attacks
param=param_4833,The Kalphite King will use abilities in between his special attacks.<br><br>If the Kalphite King is in melee form, he will use: <col=E6DCB4>Dismember, Hurricane Punish, Quake, and <col=E6DCB4>Slaughter.</col><br><br>If the Kalphite King is in Ranged form, he will use: <col=E6DCB4>Binding Shot, Ricochet, Bombardment, Fragmentation Shot, </col> and <col=E6DCB4>Incendiary Shot.</col><br><br>If the Kalphite King is in magic form, he will use: <col=E6DCB4>Wrack, Impact, Combust, Chain</col> and <col=E6DCB4>Wild Magic.</col>
param=param_4835,seq_19449
param=param_4834,npc_16697

// 30641
[struct_30641]
param=param_4832,Charge
param=param_4833,The Kalphite King charges forwards in his current direction, hitting all targets caught in his path for heavy damage, or higher damage if he slams them into a wall.
param=param_4835,seq_19457
param=param_4834,npc_16697

// 30642
[struct_30642]
param=param_4832,Beetlejuice
param=param_4833,The Kalphite King prepares to kill his main target outright, putting all of their defensive abilities on hold. Another combatant is required to <col=E6DCB4>Provoke</col> the king off of his target and then prepare to soak/avoid the incoming damage themselves through use of <col=E6DCB4>defensive abilities</col>.
param=param_4835,seq_19464
param=param_4836,seq_19465
param=param_4837,model_82793
param=param_4834,npc_16697

// 30643
[struct_30643]
param=param_4832,Knockback
param=param_4833,The Kalphite King attacks all targets directly in front of him for melee damage and knocks back those who are hit.
param=param_4835,seq_19449
param=param_4834,npc_16697

// 30644
[struct_30644]
param=param_4832,Burrow
param=param_4833,The Kalphite King burrows into the ground and disappears! Shortly after, he'll emerge from the ground where his current target is standing. Any person who is caught when he re-emerges will take large amounts of damage.
param=param_4835,seq_19451
param=param_4836,seq_19452
param=param_4837,model_82790
param=param_4834,npc_16697

// 30645
[struct_30645]
param=param_4832,Heal & Defensive Tactics
param=param_4833,If the Kalphite King is hit with a stunning attack, he will use <col=E6DCB4>Freedom.</col> Having to use freedom will also distract the king, delaying his next attack.<br><br>If the Kalphite King is hit with some ultimate abilities, he may use <col=E6DCB4>Barricade, Immortality,</col> or <col=E6DCB4>Rejuvenate</col>.<br><br>:If the Kalphite King activates a red aura, he will heal himself for all damage he deals.<br><br>If the Kalphite King activates a green aura, he will heal himself for all damage he takes.
param=param_4835,seq_19455
param=param_4836,seq_19456
param=param_4837,model_82798
param=param_4834,npc_16697

// 30646
[struct_30646]
param=param_4832,Kalphite Guardians
param=param_4833,At certain points during the fight, as the Kalphite King lowers in health, he will summon swarms of kalphite guardians, strong magic users that will defend the king with magical attacks. Players standing on the ground where a guardian has burrowed will take melee damage when they surface.
param=param_4834,npc_17156
param=param_4835,seq_19478

// 30647
[struct_30647]
param=param_4405,struct_30517
param=param_3797,1
param=param_3909,"arch_icon_digsite_guild,0"
param=param_3808,40
param=param_3807,40

// 30648
[struct_30648]
param=param_4832,Grounded Stage
param=param_4833,At the start of the fight, the Kalphite Queen is grounded and will protect from all ranged and magical attacks.  During her grounded stage she will use the <col=FFFFFF>Bite, Claw, Lightning</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Spines</col> special attacks.
param=param_4835,seq_24206
param=param_4834,npc_1158

// 30649
[struct_30649]
param=param_4832,Flying Stage
param=param_4833,After the Kalphite Queen is defeated she will hatch and begin her flying stage - in which she is immune to melee attacks.  During her flying stage she will continue to use <col=FFFFFF>Bite, Claw, Lightning</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Spines</col> special attacks.
param=param_4835,seq_24272
param=param_4834,npc_1160

// 30650
[struct_30650]
param=param_4832,Bite
param=param_4833,The Kalphite Queen bites her main target for melee damage.
param=param_4835,seq_24275
param=param_4834,npc_1158

// 30651
[struct_30651]
param=param_4832,Lightning
param=param_4833,The Kalphite Queen unleashes a barrage of lightning on all surround targets, hitting them for magical damage.
param=param_4835,seq_24281
param=param_4836,seq_24294
param=param_4837,model_97646
param=param_4834,npc_1158

// 30652
[struct_30652]
param=param_4832,Spines
param=param_4833,The Kalphite Queen launches a spine at every player nearby, hurting them with ranged damage.
param=param_4835,seq_24282
param=param_4836,seq_24286
param=param_4837,model_97643
param=param_4834,npc_1158

// 30653
[struct_30653]
param=param_4832,Melee Attacks
param=param_4833,The King Black Dragon will swipe or bite anyone who stands close to him during the fight.
param=param_4835,seq_17781

// 30654
[struct_30654]
param=param_4832,Fire Breath
param=param_4833,Being a dragon, the King Black Dragon can use extremely powerful fire breath that will destroy anyone who does not bring the appropriate anti-fire protection.
param=param_4835,seq_17786
param=param_4836,seq_17794
param=param_4837,model_76656

// 30655
[struct_30655]
param=param_4832,Frostfire Breath
param=param_4833,The King Black Dragon can use a combined attack that hits with massive fire damage while freezing his opponent in place.
param=param_4835,seq_17783
param=param_4836,seq_17790
param=param_4837,model_77901

// 30656
[struct_30656]
param=param_4832,Toxic Breath
param=param_4833,The King Black Dragon can use a combined attack that hits with massive fire damage and poisons his opponent.
param=param_4835,seq_17785
param=param_4836,seq_17792
param=param_4837,model_77900

// 30657
[struct_30657]
param=param_4832,Charged Breath
param=param_4833,The King Black Dragon can use a combined attack that hits massive fire damage and shocks his opponent, draining their skills and prayer points slightly.
param=param_4835,seq_17784
param=param_4836,seq_17788
param=param_4837,model_77899

// 30658
[struct_30658]
param=param_4832,Ranged Tornado
param=param_4833,Kree'arra fires tornadoes at nearby targets for heavy ranged damage with a chance to knockback any targets they hit. You can prevent the knockback by using the <col=E6DCB4>Anticipation</col> ability.
param=param_4835,seq_17397
param=param_4834,npc_6222
param=param_4836,seq_17364
param=param_4837,model_75294

// 30659
[struct_30659]
param=param_4832,Magic Tornado
param=param_4833,Kree'arra fires tornadoes at nearby targets for heavy Magic damage with a chance to knock back any targets they hit. You can prevent the knockback by using the <col=E6DCB4>Anticipation</col> ability.
param=param_4835,seq_17397
param=param_4834,npc_6222

// 30660
[struct_30660]
param=param_4832,Swipe
param=param_4833,Any targets who stand close to Kree'arra risk being hit by his heavy swipe attack.
param=param_4835,seq_17396
param=param_4834,npc_6222

// 30661
[struct_30661]
param=param_4832,Armadylean Bodyguards
param=param_4833,Kree'arra has backup with him in the form of <col=FFFFFF>Wingman Skree, Flockleader Geerin</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Flight Kilisa</col>. Each uses a different combat style and Kree'arra will respawn any dead bodyguards every <col=FFFFFF>30 seconds.
param=param_4835,seq_17442
param=param_4834,npc_6223

// 30662
[struct_30662]
param=param_4832,Vortex: <col=DC7800>Hard Mode Only
param=param_4833,In Hard mode, Kree'arra calls on the power of his tornadoes in full, having vortexes appear in the room. Anyone caught in a vortex will take massive magic or ranged damage dependent on the type of vortex.
param=param_4835,seq_19938
param=param_4834,npc_17097

// 30663
[struct_30663]
param=param_4832,Alignment: <col=DC7800>Hard Mode Only
param=param_4833,During Hard mode, Kree'arra will walk to the centre of the area and summon all vortexes to him. Anyone caught in the path of the tornado will take heavy damage. After Kree'arra has summoned them all to him he will disperse them again into the encounter.
param=param_4835,seq_19845
param=param_4834,npc_6222
param=param_4836,seq_19877
param=param_4837,model_84391

// 30664
[struct_30664]
param=param_4832,Slash
param=param_4833,K'ril uses his massive weapons to melee his primary target and inflict poisonous damage. If the target is protecting against melee attacks or he continues to miss he will start to get enraged.
param=param_4835,seq_14450
param=param_4834,npc_6203

// 30665
[struct_30665]
param=param_4832,Magic Slam
param=param_4833,K'ril uses his massive weapons to slam into the floor and unleash Magic damage on nearby targets. If the target is protecting against Magic attacks or he continues to miss he will start to get enraged.
param=param_4835,seq_14384
param=param_4836,seq_6947
param=param_4837,model_28221
param=param_4834,npc_6203

// 30666
[struct_30666]
param=param_4832,Prayer Destruction
param=param_4833,After K'ril has had enough of his target defending or protecting against his attacks he'll leap into the air and smash down, hitting the main target for massive damage, hitting through prayers and draining prayer points.
param=param_4835,seq_14412
param=param_4836,seq_14411
param=param_4837,model_59589
param=param_4834,npc_6203

// 30667
[struct_30667]
param=param_4832,Zamorakian Bodyguards
param=param_4833,K'ril has backup with him in the form of <col=FFFFFF>Tstanon Karlak, Zakl'n Gritch</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>Balfrug Kreeyath</col>. Each uses a different point of the combat triangle and K'ril will respawn any dead bodyguards every <col=FFFFFF>30 seconds.
param=param_4835,seq_17466
param=param_4834,npc_6204

// 30668
[struct_30668]
param=param_4832,Charge: <col=DC7800>Hard Mode only
param=param_4833,K'ril looks at his main opponent and begins charging. Anyone caught in his charge takes massive damage until he hits a wall, stopping him in his tracks.
param=param_4835,seq_19851
param=param_4834,npc_6203

// 30669
[struct_30669]
param=param_4832,Smash: <col=DC7800>Hard Mode only
param=param_4833,K'ril smashes his blade into the ground, which bursts into spikes from the impact. Standing in the spikes inflicts constant damage until the time out or you move off of them.
param=param_4835,seq_19853
param=param_4836,seq_19854
param=param_4837,model_78984
param=param_4834,npc_6203

// 30670
[struct_30670]
param=param_4832,Enrage: <col=DC7800>Hard Mode only
param=param_4833,K'ril will enrage against his opponent and go into a crazed frenzy, swinging and chasing his target wildly. Anyone caught in his wild weapons will take double damage.
param=param_4835,seq_19862
param=param_4834,npc_6203

// 30671
[struct_30671]
param=param_4832,Legio Primus
param=param_4833,Legios use strong magic attacks, firing lightning at the floor at any targets who aren't moving.<br><br>Legio Primus will <col=FFFFFF>get stronger</col> as his life points decrease.
param=param_4835,seq_20235
param=param_4834,npc_17149

// 30672
[struct_30672]
param=param_4832,Legio Secundus
param=param_4833,Legios use strong magic attacks, firing lightning at the floor at any targets who aren't moving.<br><br>Legio Secundus will fire his lightning attack more often than his regular attacks as his life points get lower.
param=param_4835,seq_20235
param=param_4834,npc_17150

// 30673
[struct_30673]
param=param_4832,Legio Tertius
param=param_4833,Legios use strong magic attacks, firing lightning at the floor at any targets who aren't moving.<br><br>Legio Tertius will summon <col=FFFFFF>rorarii, gladii</col>, and <col=FFFFFF>capsarii</col> as his life points lower to aid him.
param=param_4835,seq_20235
param=param_4834,npc_17151

// 30674
[struct_30674]
param=param_4832,Legio Quartus
param=param_4833,Legios use strong magic attacks, firing lightning at the floor at any targets who aren't moving.<br><br>As his life points are lowered, Legio Quartus will <col=FFFFFF>teleport</col> all targets straight towards him and fire an extra blast of lightning.
param=param_4835,seq_20235
param=param_4834,npc_17152

// 30675
[struct_30675]
param=param_4832,Legio Quintus
param=param_4833,Legios use strong magic attacks, firing lightning at the floor at any targets who aren't moving.<br><br>As his lifepoints are lowered, Legio Quintus can create <col=FFFFFF>Lines of Ascension</col> that draw across the arena and hurt anyone who dares cross them.
param=param_4835,seq_20235
param=param_4834,npc_17153

// 30676
[struct_30676]
param=param_4832,Legio Sextus
param=param_4833,Legios use strong magic attacks, firing lightning at the floor at any targets who aren't moving.<br><br>Legio Sextus's lightning attack is far larger and lasts longer, making him a very potent legio.
param=param_4835,seq_20235
param=param_4834,npc_17154

// 30677
[struct_30677]
param=param_4832,Melee Swipe
param=param_4833,Throughout the encounter, Nex will use a powerful sweeping melee attack against any targets within melee distance to her. <br><br>On her Zaros phase, Nex's melee attack will be expanded to a frontal cone.
param=param_4835,seq_17453
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30678
[struct_30678]
param=param_4832,Smoke Magic
param=param_4833,During smoke phase, Nex will fire a barrage of smoky projectiles to all surrounding targets, hitting magical damage. There is also a chance Nex will use this attack to poison you, or pull you towards her if you haven't anticipated the attack.
param=param_4835,seq_17413
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30679
[struct_30679]
param=param_4832,Choke
param=param_4833,Nex will infect one target with a virus. As that target coughs the virus away, they will infect any other targets adjacent to them. Every cough of the virus lowers combat stats.
param=param_4835,seq_17414
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30680
[struct_30680]
param=param_4832,Smoke bullet
param=param_4833,Nex will align with Zaros, picking a path in the chamber to teleport to and firing herself forward to the centre. Any targets caught in the path or centre will be forced forward by her attack, taking massive damage.
param=param_4835,seq_17411
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30681
[struct_30681]
param=param_4832,Fumus
param=param_4833,When Nex drops below <col=FFFFFF>80% life points</col> she will call on Fumus to aid her. Until this point, Fumus is invulnerable. If Fumus is killed, Nex will move onto the next stage, calling on the power of Shadow.
param=param_4835,seq_17399
param=param_4834,npc_13451

// 30682
[struct_30682]
param=param_4832,Shadow Shot
param=param_4833,During the Shadow phase, Nex will use the power of shadow to fling ranged projectiles at all surrounding targets.
param=param_4835,seq_17413
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30683
[struct_30683]
param=param_4832,Shadow Smash
param=param_4833,Nex will find all nearby victims and put a deadly shadow below them. Shortly after placing the shadows, they will erupt, hitting heavy damage on anyone caught in the dark.
param=param_4835,seq_17407
param=param_4836,seq_17368
param=param_4837,model_75424
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30684
[struct_30684]
param=param_4832,Embrace Darkness
param=param_4833,Nex will plunge her targets into darkness, making it darker the closer targets are to her. If any targets are too close to Nex for too long they will become engulfed in shadow, taking constant damage from the pure shadow.
param=param_4835,seq_17412
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30685
[struct_30685]
param=param_4832,Umbra
param=param_4833,When Nex drops below <col=FFFFFF>60% life points</col> she will call on Umbra to aid her. Until this point, Umbra is invulnerable. If Umbra is killed, Nex will move onto the next stage, calling on the power of blood.
param=param_4835,seq_17399
param=param_4834,npc_13452

// 30686
[struct_30686]
param=param_4832,Blood Siphon
param=param_4833,Nex will use her wings to shield her from damage and siphon it to heal her. Any damage over time effects placed on Nex during blood phase will also heal her.<br><br>Any <col=FFFFFF>Blood reavers</col> that are alive when Blood siphon starts will die and transfer their life points to Nex.
param=param_4835,seq_17409
param=param_4836,seq_17375
param=param_4837,model_6230
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30687
[struct_30687]
param=param_4832,Blood Reavers
param=param_4833,When Nex begins <col=FFFFFF>Blood Siphon</col>, she will also summon blood reavers to the arena. Any blood reavers that survive until the next <col=FFFFFF>Blood Siphon</col> will transfer their life points to Nex.
param=param_4835,seq_7008
param=param_4834,npc_13458

// 30688
[struct_30688]
param=param_4832,Blood Barrage
param=param_4833,During the Blood phase, Nex will shoot Blood Barrage on her targets, healing a percentage of any damage it inflicts on them.
param=param_4835,seq_17414
param=param_4836,seq_17378
param=param_4837,model_75304
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30689
[struct_30689]
param=param_4832,Blood Sacrifice
param=param_4833,Nex will mark a target for sacrifice. This target has <col=FFFFFF>4 seconds</col> to get as far away from Nex as possible. If they do not manage to get far enough, Nex heals dramatically and instantly fires another <col=FFFFFF>Blood Barrage.</col>
param=param_4835,seq_17414
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30690
[struct_30690]
param=param_4832,Cruor
param=param_4833,When Nex drops below <col=FFFFFF>40% life points</col> she will call on Cruor to aid her. Until this point, Cruor is invulnerable. If Cruor is killed, Nex will move onto the next stage, calling on the power of ice.
param=param_4835,seq_17399
param=param_4834,npc_13453

// 30691
[struct_30691]
param=param_4832,Ice Prison
param=param_4833,Nex will put her target in a prison of ice. Other players have <col=FFFFFF>6 seconds</col> to free her prisoner before the ice shatters for massive damage. Other combatants can free the imprisoned player by destroying the icicles surrounding them.
param=param_4835,seq_17414
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30692
[struct_30692]
param=param_4832,Ice Barrage
param=param_4833,During the Ice phase, Nex will use Ice Barrage against her targets, freezing them in place. Protection from Magic will help reduce damage and freezing effects, but will also increase prayer drain.
param=param_4835,seq_17414
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30693
[struct_30693]
param=param_4832,Containment
param=param_4833,Nex smashes the floor, creating surround icicles that damage anyone caught next to her. Half of the icicles then being moving towards their assigned targets, hitting anyone caught in their way until the stop.
param=param_4835,seq_17407
param=param_4836,seq_17368
param=param_4837,model_75424
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30694
[struct_30694]
param=param_4832,Glacies
param=param_4833,When Nex drops below <col=FFFFFF>20% life points</col> she will call on Glacies to aid her. Until this point, Glacies is invulnerable. If Glacies is killed, Nex will move onto the next stage, calling on the power of Zaros himself.
param=param_4835,seq_17399
param=param_4834,npc_13454

// 30695
[struct_30695]
param=param_4832,Power of Zaros
param=param_4833,Nex calls on Zaros himself to empower her, This heals her, and increases her damage and accuracy for the remainder of her life. She will then cycle between using <col=FFFFFF>Soulsplit, Deflect Melee,</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Leech</col> curses against her opponents.<br><br>During the Zaros phase, Nex's melee attacks become area-of-effect, hitting anyone within <col=FFFFFF>1 metre</col> of her primary target.
param=param_4835,seq_17410
param=param_4836,seq_17377
param=param_4837,model_6702
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30696
[struct_30696]
param=param_4832,Wrath
param=param_4833,When Nex is defeated, she'll activate the <col=FFFFFF>Wrath</col> curse, hitting anyone with an explosion who is nearby where she perishes.
param=param_4835,seq_17415
param=param_4834,npc_13447

// 30697
[struct_30697]
param=param_4832,Deflection
param=param_4833,During the fight, Nex can randomly decide to use a deflection curse <col=FFFFFF>(ranged or magic)</col> for <col=FFFFFF>2 minutes</col>. This becomes more probable as the phases carry on. She will only use one type per kill and will alternate between the two as kills go on.

// 30698
[struct_30698]
param=param_4832,Artefacts
param=param_4833,The Queen Black Dragon cannot be defeated, only returned to slumber. To do this, you must activate <col=FFFFFF>four artefacts</col> that become enabled when the Queen Black Dragon reaches <col=FFFFFF>0 life points</col>.
param=param_4834,npc_15454

// 30699
[struct_30699]
param=param_4832,Melee/Range Attack
param=param_4833,The Queen Black Dragon will use a powerful swipe to any targets found at the front of her platform causing <col=FFFFFF>ranged</col> damage, if the target stands melee distance she will resort to biting them if they are completely adjacent.
param=param_4835,seq_16720
param=param_4834,npc_15454

// 30700
[struct_30700]
param=param_4832,Fire Breath
param=param_4833,The Queen Black Dragon can unleash massive fire breath at any point throughout the fight. Those who do not bring appropriate anti-fire protection will burn for incredible damage.
param=param_4835,seq_16721
param=param_4834,npc_15454

// 30701
[struct_30701]
param=param_4832,Wall of Fire
param=param_4833,The Queen Black Dragon summons a massive wall of fire which passes over the platform inflicting fire damage. Keep an eye out for a weak point in the wall that you can pass through unharmed.<br><br>Based on the fights duration, the Queen Black Dragon may summon up to <col=FFFFFF>three walls of fire</col> at the same time.
param=param_4835,seq_16746
param=param_4836,seq_16762
param=param_4837,model_69671
param=param_4834,npc_15454

// 30702
[struct_30702]
param=param_4832,Convulsion
param=param_4833,After the Queen Black Dragon has been defeated, you need to activate the next appropriate <col=FFFFFF>artefact</col>. While vulnerable, the queen will fire out <col=FFFFFF>grotworms</col> until the <col=FFFFFF>artefact</col> is enabled. These grotworms attack the player with magic, and they will stay until the rest of the fight.
param=param_4835,seq_16722
param=param_4834,npc_15454

// 30703
[struct_30703]
param=param_4832,Tortured souls
param=param_4833,From <col=FFFFFF>Stage two</col> onwards, the Queen Black Dragon will spawn increasing amounts of <col=FFFFFF>Tortured souls</col>. Tortured souls will fire <col=FFFFFF>arcane waves</col> along the floor towards their target. <br><br>If they hit a different target on the way, they will disperse - otherwise they hit their target for unblockable damage.
param=param_4835,seq_16883
param=param_4834,npc_15510

// 30704
[struct_30704]
param=param_4832,Time Stop
param=param_4833,A <col=FFFFFF>Tortured souls</col> may start chanting a ritual that will result in time stopping temporarily. If the spell completes, the target cannot move or act, but will suffer time stopping for <col=FFFFFF>10 seconds</col>, after which everything the Queen Black Dragon has done will be instantly applied.
param=param_4834,npc_15454

// 30705
[struct_30705]
param=param_4832,Forging Fire
param=param_4833,Forging Fire is the ultimate fire breath attack the Queen Black Dragon will unleash in stage four. Any target standing in the centre of the fire will take massive fire damage. Note that this is enough heat to forge the <col=FFFFFF>royal crossbow</col>. <br><br>Targets on the outskirts of the fire take less damage.
param=param_4835,seq_16745
param=param_4836,seq_16749
param=param_4837,model_69669
param=param_4834,npc_15454

// 30706
[struct_30706]
param=param_4832,Crystal Form
param=param_4833,The Queen Black Dragon takes on the consistency of crystal. She is more resistant to magic, but weaker to physical damage for <col=FFFFFF>50 seconds, or until the next artefact is enabled.
param=param_4835,seq_16715
param=param_4834,npc_15506

// 30707
[struct_30707]
param=param_4832,Hardened Carapace
param=param_4833,The Queen Black Dragon hardens her carapace. She is more resistant to physical damage, but more vulnerable to magic for <col=FFFFFF>50 seconds, or until the next artefact is enabled.
param=param_4835,seq_16715
param=param_4834,npc_15507

// 30708
[struct_30708]
param=param_4832,Melee Swipe
param=param_4833,TzTok-Jad has only one focus: killing his target. Expect to die if you do not protect against his massive melee attack. TzTok-Jad will only use melee swipe when the target gets within melee distance.
param=param_4835,seq_16204
param=param_4834,npc_2745

// 30709
[struct_30709]
param=param_4832,Ranged Smash
param=param_4833,TzTok-Jad has only one focus: killing his target. Expect to die if you do not protect against his massive ranged attack.
param=param_4835,seq_16202
param=param_4836,seq_16203
param=param_4837,model_65639
param=param_4834,npc_2745

// 30710
[struct_30710]
param=param_4832,Magic Death
param=param_4833,TzTok-Jad has only one focus: killing his target. Expect to die if you do not protect against his massive magic attack.
param=param_4835,seq_16195
param=param_4836,seq_16196
param=param_4837,model_65646
param=param_4834,npc_2745

// 30711
[struct_30711]
param=param_4832,Medic!
param=param_4833,When TzTok-Jad passes <col=FFFFFF>50% life points</col> he calls multiple Yt-HurKot's towards him, all with the aim of healing him. If kept unchecked, they will continually heal him for the duration of the encounter.
param=param_4835,seq_16084
param=param_4834,npc_2746

// 30712
[struct_30712]
param=param_4832,Maul of Omens
param=param_4833,Vorago can only be defeated via use of the <col=FFFFFF>Maul of Omens</col>. This weapon can be assembled during the fight. Parts are found in <col=FFFFFF>stages 1, 2, and 4</col>.

// 30713
[struct_30713]
param=param_4832,Melee Swipe
param=param_4833,Vorago hits his main target and swipes them for heavy melee damage. Having another tank in the vicinity can help lower the damage. Anyone adjacent to Vorago will also be hit.
param=param_4835,seq_20355
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30714
[struct_30714]
param=param_4832,Magic Bomb
param=param_4833,The Magic Bomb is a magic attack that will attempt to target the furthest player away, multiple magic bombs will be fired at once should there be a large number of players fighting Vorago.
param=param_4835,seq_20356
param=param_4836,seq_20357
param=param_4837,model_86780
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30715
[struct_30715]
param=param_4832,Explosive bomb
param=param_4833,Vorago picks a target (preferring the farthest player away) and fires an explosive bomb towards them. On impact it detonates for significant damage - more so if multiple targets are in the explosive area.
param=param_4835,seq_20371
param=param_4836,seq_20372
param=param_4837,model_86775
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30716
[struct_30716]
param=param_4405,struct_30517
param=param_3797,2
param=param_3909,"arch_icon_digsite_guild,1"
param=param_3808,40
param=param_3807,40

// 30717
[struct_30717]
param=param_4832,Jump-Smash
param=param_4833,At the end of each stage, Vorago will jump up and smash down in another location. Anyone caught in proximity to him landing risks taking heavy damage. After <col=FFFFFF>three smashes</col> the floor will give way and everyone will fall deeper into the encounter.
param=param_4835,seq_20365
param=param_4836,seq_20366
param=param_4837,model_86779
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30718
[struct_30718]
param=param_4832,Destroy Tank
param=param_4833,Vorago performs a strong melee attack against his main target <col=FFFFFF>five times</col> in a row. Each attack will place a damage-over-time effect on the target, which persists if they are close to Vorago.<br><br>If the damage-over-time effect exists on Vorago's target when he attacks them again, the target will suffer a massive melee hit.<br><br>Using abilities such as <col=FFFFFF>Provoke</col> and <col=FFFFFF>Freedom</col> should be considered to deal with this attack.
param=param_4835,seq_20363
param=param_4836,seq_20364
param=param_4837,model_86777
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30719
[struct_30719]
param=param_4832,Target Link
param=param_4833,Vorago picks a target and links himself to them for <col=FFFFFF>10 seconds</col>. During this time, any damage done to Vorago is instead applied to the linked target.
param=param_4835,seq_20319
param=param_4836,seq_20320
param=param_4837,model_86784
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30720
[struct_30720]
param=param_4832,Gravity Fields
param=param_4833,Vorago will spawn gravity fields in stage two. If a gravity field is activated and Vorago is nearby, it'll fly towards him. After Vorago has absorbed <col=FFFFFF>4 gravity fields (2 if players fail the next stage)</col> he will be destabilised and can be brought down.

// 30721
[struct_30721]
param=param_4832,Bring Him Down!
param=param_4833,After Vorago has absorbed <col=FFFFFF>4 gravity fields</col> all targets will become linked to Vorago and gravity itself. Opponents are then required to attack Vorago repeatedly to pull him into the floor, leaving him vulnerable.
param=param_4835,null
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30722
[struct_30722]
param=param_4832,Destroy Phase
param=param_4833,After Vorago has been pulled into the floor, he will be idle and vulnerable for <col=FFFFFF>10 seconds</col>. During this time his opponents have to deal massive damage to obtain the piece of the <col=FFFFFF>Maul of Omens.</col><br><br>If this is failed, you are required to repeat the <col=FFFFFF>gravity fields</col> once again.
param=param_4835,seq_20361
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30723
[struct_30723]
param=param_4832,Stage 3
param=param_4833,Stage 3 is a special case. The chasm Vorago falls into may change week on week. Be prepared for any of the following!

// 30724
[struct_30724]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.1 : Ceiling rotation
param=param_4833,Vorago will fire a projectile at the sky and follow it up. Shortly after a shadow will appear on the floor and the section of ceiling will fall down and smash anyone found underneath it. Slowly the entire arena may become blocked off if left unchecked.
param=param_4835,seq_20369
param=param_4836,seq_20370
param=param_4837,model_86780
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30725
[struct_30725]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.1 : Ceiling detonation
param=param_4833,If the arena is becoming locked down due to the <col=FFFFFF>ceiling collapse</col>, Vorago's opponents can choose to destroy the debris, but will take heavy damage in the process. Any leftover debris will also fall through into the next stage.

// 30726
[struct_30726]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.2 : Scopulus
param=param_4833,Scopuli are all tied to each other in spirit. The closer these creatures are to each other, the more accuracy and damage they will do, as well as increasing the distance they will inflict damage on their targets.
param=param_4835,seq_20339
param=param_4834,npc_17185

// 30727
[struct_30727]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.2 : Scopulus Enrage
param=param_4833,When a scopulus dies, it will heal its linked scopulus for <col=FFFFFF>10% of its life points</col> as well as enrage it - increasing its damage, accuracy, attack speed and attack spread.
param=param_4835,seq_20344
param=param_4834,npc_17185

// 30728
[struct_30728]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.3 : Summon Vitalii
param=param_4833,Vorago will pick an area in the arena and fire a shockwave towards it. When the shockwave arrives, multiple <col=FFFFFF>vitalii</col> may spawn. To counteract this, you can have a person stand in the shockwave to prevent a <col=FFFFFF>vitalis</col> spawning, taking some damage instead.
param=param_4835,seq_20328
param=param_4836,seq_20329
param=param_4837,model_86774
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30729
[struct_30729]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.3 : Vitalii
param=param_4833,Vitalii will attack anyone near to themselves or Vorago, hitting quickly for melee damage.
param=param_4835,seq_20378
param=param_4834,npc_17157

// 30730
[struct_30730]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.4 : Gas Bomb
param=param_4833,Vorago fires a green bomb at a random area in the encounter. On impact it will create a <col=FFFFFF>Gas cloud</col> as well as bouncing towards a target. When it hits this target it will look to bounce again to another target.<br>Each unique target will take damage when it bounces to them.<br><br>If no targets are found, the bomb will explode immediately for massive damage.<br><br>If the bomb hits the same target twice it will detonate for heavy damage.
param=param_4835,seq_20356
param=param_4836,seq_20357
param=param_4837,model_89920
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30731
[struct_30731]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.4 : Gas cloud
param=param_4833,Standing in a gas cloud will drain run energy, <col=FFFFFF>adrenaline</col> and life points consistently.

// 30732
[struct_30732]
param=param_4832,Stage 3.5 : Teamsplit
param=param_4833,Vorago will try to split the team in two. Half of the team will be marked as green and the other half red. Vorago also places coloured zones in the room and begins charging for <col=FFFFFF>8 seconds</col>.After this time, anyone not standing in the matching zone will explode for massive damage.
param=param_4835,seq_20322
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30733
[struct_30733]
param=param_4832,Stage 4 : Waterfall
param=param_4833,Vorago will open a waterfall from above and teleport to the centre of the encounter to begin charging. <col=FFFFFF>10 seconds later</col>, he will explode for massive fire damage. Anyone not hiding behind a waterfall will suffer massive damage from the fire.
param=param_4835,seq_20323
param=param_4836,seq_20324
param=param_4837,model_86781
param=param_4834,npc_17182

// 30734
[struct_30734]
param=param_4832,Stage 4 : Stone clones
param=param_4833,Vorago will show some of his opponents stone versions of themselves. Each will have to defeat their stone clone, which will use a full suite of <col=FFFFFF>combat abilities</col>. If you defeat a clone, you may help team mates who also have stone clones.
param=param_4835,seq_18015
param=param_4834,npc_17158

// 30735
[struct_30735]
param=param_4832,Stage 5 : Finale
param=param_4833,In the final stage of the fight, opponents must face off against Vorago in a race of damage.<br><br>As Vorago inflicts damage, he will push his opponents <col=FFFFFF>west</col>. If the team is pushed off of the platform, they all suffer <col=FFFFFF>instant death.</col>.<br><br>As the team damages Vorago, he will be pushed. <col=FFFFFF>east.</col> If the team gets Vorago to the far end of the platform, he will be vulnerable to the <col=FFFFFF>Maul of Omens</col> which can be used to finish him off.
param=param_4835,null
param=param_4834,npc_17182

