// 45410
[struct_45410]
param=param_4832,Kerapac
param=param_4833,Fighting under the control of Jas, Kerapac is an extremely powerful dragonkin who wields multiple elder artefacts and will stop at nothing to achieve his goal.

// 45411
[struct_45411]
param=param_4832,Time-threads
param=param_4833,When a player gets close to defeating Kerapac, he communes with the time altering elder artefact, the Needle. Using this power, Kerapac rewinds time and starts his onslaught again.<br><br>By doing so, he creates a new Time-thread. A version of Kerapac existing within the previous Time-thread will appear and attacks from the previous phases will play out at the same time during this new Time-thread.

// 45412
[struct_45412]
param=param_4832,Shatter
param=param_4833,Kerapac will smash his staff into the ground, causing a powerful attack to charge toward the player. The force of this hit can stun the player if they're struck by it.<br><br>Once the attack reaches the edges of the arena, Kerapac will draw it back toward him, causing any player caught in the crossfire to take a large amount of damage.<br><br>In Hard Mode, the force of Kerapac's attack will rip a hole in the current time thread which will seep damage to all players in the arena until closed.
param=param_4835,seq_34198

// 45413
[struct_45413]
param=param_4832,Jumping slam
param=param_4833,Kerapac will jump up and hover in the air for a few seconds before slamming back toward the ground focused on where his target is currently.<br><br>If Kerapac lands on his target, he will pin them in place and apply continuous damage until they break free of his pin. Using the ability <col=E6DCB4>Freedom</col> or <col=E6DCB4>Anticipation</col> will stop Kerapac being able to pin you in place.<br><br>Kerapac will jump <col=FFFFFF>3 times</col> before resuming his attacks.
param=param_4835,seq_34193

// 45414
[struct_45414]
param=param_4832,Lightning strike
param=param_4833,Kerapac will call upon the power of the Staff of Armadyl to cause a torrent of lightning waves to sweep across the arena.
param=param_4835,seq_34197

// 45415
[struct_45415]
param=param_4832,Hard Mode - Overcharge
param=param_4833,In Hard Mode, Kerapac will push the needle one step too far, causing it to overcharge and cross over the Time-threads that Kerapac created previously.<br><br>An echo of Kerapac from each phase, along with an echo of the player will appear.<br><br>Kerapac, now tethering his life from the broken Time-threads, becomes immune to incoming attacks until the echos have been dealt with.<br><br>During this phase, Kerapac will be attacking all players with a barrage of powerful attacks.
param=param_4835,seq_34201
param=param_4836,seq_34218

// 45416
[struct_45416]
param=param_4832,Hard Mode - Fury
param=param_4833,In Hard Mode, all versions of Kerapac have a stacking buff called <col=E6DCB4>Fury</col>. For each stack, Kerapac gains a <col=FFFFFF>1%</col> damage increase for all attacks.

// 45417
[struct_45417]
param=param_4832,Hard Mode - Echoes
param=param_4833,For each Time-thread, an echo of the player exists and is being targeted by an echo of Kerapac.<br><br>If Kerapac kills a player's echo, all versions of Kerapac gain <col=FFFFFF>25 stacks</col> of Fury. A player can jump into a Time-thread and then heal their echo up. Jumping into a Time-thread will cause the appropriate echo of Kerapac to start targeting the player.<br><br>Defeating an echo of Kerapac will lower the main Kerapac's shield but will also cause all versions of Kerapac to gain <col=FFFFFF>50 stacks</col> of Fury.
param=param_4834,npc_28076

